AB  - (no language specified) ArmTeX is a system for typesetting Armenian text with Plain TeX or LaTeX(2e). It may be used with input:

      
      + from a standard Latin keyboard without any special encoding and/or support for Armenian letters,
      + from any keyboard which uses an encoding that has Armenian letters in the second half (characters 128-255) 
        of the extended ASCII table (for example ArmSCII8 Armenian standard),
      + from an Armenian keyboard using UTF-8 encoding.
Users should note that the manuals still mostly describe the previous version of the package (ArmTeX 
      2.0). However, a description of the new features of ArmTeX 3.0 is provided at the end of the README file.
