TY  - ICOMM
UR  - https://ctan.org/pkg/boolexpr
Y3  - 2025-02-07
T1  - boolexpr
T2  - A boolean expression evaluator and a switch command
AU  - Chervet, Florent
AB  - (no language specified) The  \boolexpr macro evaluates boolean expressions in a purely expandable way.

       \boolexpr{ A \OR B \AND C } expands to 0 if the logical expression is TRUE. A, B, C may be: numeric 
      expressions such as: x=y , x<>y , x>y or x<y ;
– boolean switches: \iftrue 
      0\else 1\fi ;
– conditionals: \ifcsname whatsit\endcsname 0\else 1\fi ;
– another \boolexpr : \boolexpr{ 
      D \OR E \AND F }: 

       \boolexpr may be used with \ifcase: 
 |
\ifcase\boolexpr{ A \OR B \AND C }
What to do if true
\else
What to do if false
\fi
| 

      The  \switch command (which is also expandable) has the form: |
\switch
\case{<boolean expression>} ...
\case{<boolean expression>} ...
...
\otherwise ...
\endswitch
|
UR  - https://ctan.org/tex-archive/macros/latex/contrib/boolexpr/boolexpr.pdf
