AB  - (no language specified) The package essentially just wraps a minipage within an  \fbox . However, while \fbox{\begin{minipage}{\linewidth}...\end{minipage}} juts 
      out into the margin, \begin{boxedminipage}...\end{boxedminipage} does not. Instead, it subtracts 
      the frame’s dimensions from the specified dimensions of the minipage before typesetting the minipage.

      Note: The package was formerly known as  boxedminipage2e and now 'replaces' Mario Wolczko’s 
      earlier boxedminipage package.
