TY  - ICOMM
UR  - https://ctan.org/pkg/cellspace
Y3  - 2026-04-10
T1  - cellspace
T2  - Ensure minimal spacing of table cells
AU  - Noirel, Josselin
Y2  - 2026-01-24
PY  - 2026
AB  - (no language specified) It is well known that high or deep cells tend to touch the  \hline s of a tabular . This 
      package provides a modifier S acting on usual column types so that to ensure a minimal distance 
      that can be controlled through two parameters \cellspacetoplimit and \cellspacebottomlimit .

      The approach employed by this package is noticeably simpler than that of  tabls (https://ctan.org/pkg/tabls) , 
      which considers the dimensions of each entire row; whereas you can ask the cellspace only to look at 
      the cells of potentially difficult columns.

      The package depends on  ifthen (https://ctan.org/pkg/ifthen) , array (https://ctan.org/pkg/array) , calc 
      (https://ctan.org/pkg/calc) , and xkeyval (https://ctan.org/pkg/xkeyval) .
