AB  - (no language specified) CID-keyed fonts were developed by Adobe to handle character sets containing large numbers of glyphs, 
      notably for East Asian languages (Chinese, Japanese, Korean, etc.). The glyphs are addressed by number 
      rather than name, and organized into so-called collections.

      Several of Adobe’s CID mapping files are distributed as part of  ConTeXt (https://ctan.org/pkg/context) . 
      In TeX Live (https://ctan.org/pkg/texlive) , they are in the directory texmf-dist/fonts/cid .

      See the  Wikipedia entry (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PostScript_fonts#CID) , among other places, 
      for more information.
