AB  - (no language specified) The Clojure pamphlet system is a system based on the Clojure literate system. In the Clojure's pamphlet 
      system you have your main LaTeX file, which can be compiled regularly. This file contains documentation 
      and source code (just like in other forms of literate programming). These code snippets are wrapped in 
      the  chunk environment, hence they can be recognized by the tangler in order to extract them. 
      Chunks can be included inside each other by the getchunk command (which will be typesetted acordingly). 
      Finally, the LaTeX file will be run through the tangler to get the desired chunk of code.
