T1  - cm
T2  - Computer Modern fonts
AU  - Knuth, Donald E.
AB  - (no language specified) Knuth's final iteration of his re-interpretation of a c.19 Modern-style font from Monotype. The family 
      is comprehensive, offering both sans and roman styles, and a monospaced font, together with mathematics 
      fonts closely integrated with the mathematical facilities of TeX itself.

      The base fonts are distributed as  Metafont source (https://ctan.org/pkg/cm-mf) , but autotraced 
      PostScript Type 1 versions are available (one version in the AMS fonts (https://ctan.org/pkg/amsfonts) distribution, 
      and also the BaKoMa (https://ctan.org/pkg/bakoma-fonts) distribution).

      The Computer Modern fonts have inspired many later families, notably the  European Computer Modern 
      (https://ctan.org/pkg/ec) and the Latin Modern (https://ctan.org/pkg/lm) families.
