AU  - Downes, Michael J.
AB  - (no language specified) The package keeps track of whether a command defined in a document preamble is actually used somewhere 
      in the document. After the package is loaded in the preamble of a document, all  \newcommand (and 
      similar command definitions) between that point and the beginning of the document will be marked for 
      logging. At the end of the document a report of command usage will be printed in the TeX log, for example:

      
      + “ mdash was used on line 25 ”;
      + “ ndash was never used ”.
