Y3  - 2025-02-07
T1  - csvtools
T2  - Reading data from CSV files
AU  - Talbot, Nicola
AB  - (no language specified) The csvtools package allows you to repeatedly perform a set of LaTeX commands on data in each row of 
      a comma separated variable (CSV) file (though substitution of the ‘comma’ is permitted). Such files may 
      be used as source for mail merging, generating tables etc. Examples are given in the documentation.

      The distribution also provides packages:

      +  csvsort , that provides analagous commands to those in the main package, having first sorted the 
        data (using the xfor (https://ctan.org/pkg/xfor) and compare (https://ctan.org/pkg/compare) packages); 
        and
      +  csvpie , for creating a pie-chart from a CSV file.
The bundle has now been superseded by the  datatool (https://ctan.org/pkg/datatool) bundle.
