AB  - (no language specified) This package is used in concert with the  cyber (https://ctan.org/pkg/cyber) package to make documents 
      with annotations of compliance with cybersecurity requirements. “cic” stands for “Controls in Contents”, 
      and when you include this package, some notations of compliance are added to section names as seen in 
      the table of contents of the final document.

      It also makes your document more brittle in unexpected ways: for example, when you use  cybercic in 
      the same document as hyperref (https://ctan.org/pkg/hyperref) , you cannot use any formatting in 
      your section titles. So don't use cybercic unless you need to.
