AB  - (no language specified) These macros provide a method of locally allocating registers without interference with previously allocated 
      registers; thus  \declarecount allocates a count for local use, in exactly the same way that \newcount allocations 
      one for global use. The sequence

       |
{... \declarecount\foo ... \newcount\bar ...}
| is of course a logical error; any  \new* command should be issued before the corresponding \declare* command.
