T1  - dosepsbin
T2  - Deal with DOS binary EPS files
AU  - Oberdiek, Heiko
AB  - (no language specified) A Encapsulated PostScript (EPS) file may given in a special binary format to support the inclusion of 
      a thumbnail. This file format, commonly known as  'DOS EPS' format starts with a binary header 
      that contains the positions of the possible sections:

      + PostScript (PS);
      + Windows Metafile Format (WMF); and
      + Tag Image File Format (TIFF).
The PS section must be present and either the WMF file or the TIFF file should be given.

      The package provides a Perl program that will extract any of the sections of such a file, in particular 
      providing a ‘text’-form EPS file for use with (La)TeX.
UR  - https://ctan.org/tex-archive/support/dosepsbin/dosepsbin.pdf
