Y3  - 2025-02-07
T1  - dot2tex
T2  - Convert graphs generated by Graphviz to LaTeX friendly formats
AU  - Fauske, Kjell Magne
AB  - (no language specified) Dot2tex is a tool for converting graphs rendered by Graphviz to formats that can be used with LaTeX.

      The purpose of dot2tex is to give graphs generated by Graphviz a more LaTeX friendly look and feel. This 
      is accomplished by converting xdot output from Graphviz to a series of  TikZ and PGF (https://ctan.org/pkg/pgf) , 
      or PSTricks (https://ctan.org/pkg/pstricks-base) commands. This approach allows:

      + Typesetting labels with LaTeX, allowing mathematical notation;
      + Using native PSTricks and PGF/TikZ commands for drawing arrows; and
      + Using backend specific styles to customize the output.
Dot2tex requires a Python interpreter v2.4 or better.
UR  - https://ctan.org/tex-archive/graphics/dot2tex/README
