TY  - ICOMM
UR  - https://ctan.org/pkg/emp
Y3  - 2025-02-07
T1  - emp
T2  - "Encapsulate" MetaPost figures in a document
AU  - Ohl, Thorsten
AB  - (no language specified) Emp is a package for encapsulating  MetaPost (https://ctan.org/pkg/metapost) figures in LaTeX: 
      the package provides environments where you can place MetaPost commands, and means of using that code 
      as fragments for building up figures to include in your document. So, with emp, the procedure is to run 
      your document with LaTeX, run MetaPost, and then complete running your document in the normal way.

      Emp is therefore useful for keeping illustrations in synchrony with the text. It also frees you from 
      inventing descriptive names for PostScript files that fit into the confines of file system conventions.
UR  - https://ctan.org/tex-archive/macros/latex/contrib/emp/README
