AB  - (no language specified) Inria is a free font designed by  Black[Foundry] (https://black-foundry.com/) for Inria research 
      institute. The font is available for free. It comes as Serif and Sans Serif, each with three weights 
      and matching italics.

      Using these fonts with XeLaTeX and LuaLaTeX is easy using the  fontspec (https://ctan.org/pkg/fontspec) package; 
      we refer to the documentation of fontspec (https://ctan.org/pkg/fontspec) for more information.

      The present package provides a way of using them with LaTeX and pdfLaTeX: it provides two style files, 
       InriaSerif.sty and InriaSans.sty , together with the PostScript version of the fonts and 
      their associated files. These were created using autoinst.
