TY  - ICOMM
UR  - https://ctan.org/pkg/interval
Y3  - 2025-02-07
T1  - interval
T2  - Format mathematical intervals, ensuring proper spacing
AU  - Madsen, Lars
Y2  - 2019-03-06
PY  - 2019
AB  - (no language specified) When typing an open interval as  $]a,b[$ , a closing bracket is being used in place of an opening 
      fence and vice versa. This leads to the wrong spacing in, say, $]-a,b[$ or $A\in]a,b[=B$ . The 
      package attempts to solve this using:
 \interval{a}{b} -> [a,b] 
 \interval[open]{a}{b} -> ]a,b[ 
 \interval[open 
      left]{a}{b} -> ]a,b] 

      The package also supports fence scaling and ensures that the enclosing fences will end up having the 
      proper closing and opening types. TeX maths does not do this job properly.

      The package depends on  pgfkeys (https://ctan.org/pkg/pgfkeys) .
UR  - https://ctan.org/tex-archive/macros/latex/contrib/interval/interval.pdf
L1  - C:\Users\guent\Documents\python\CTAN2\7434102523-interval.pdf
