T1  - jj-game
T2  - A LaTeX class to construct Jeopardy-like games
AU  - Story, Donald P.
Y2  - 2016-11-24
PY  - 2016
AB  - (no language specified) The class defines a Jeopardy-like game; question answers may be multiple choice, or text or mathematics 
      ‘fill-ins’.

      The basic game can be constructed using dvipsone,  dvips (https://ctan.org/pkg/dvips) , pdftex 
      (https://ctan.org/pkg/pdftex) or dvipdfm (https://ctan.org/pkg/dvipdfm) . The ‘pro’ option of 
      the game works with dvipsone or dvips only, and requires Adobe Acrobat Pro 7.0 (or later), with its distiller.

      The game requires the  AcroTeX education bundle (https://ctan.org/pkg/acrotex) , and (for the pro 
      option) AeB pro (https://ctan.org/pkg/aeb-pro) .

      Also, the  eforms (https://ctan.org/pkg/eforms) package dated 2016-08-29 or later is required.

      Samples of sources for games are provided.
