AB  - (no language specified) LaTeX is a widely-used macro package for TeX, providing many basic document formating commands extended 
      by a wide range of packages. It is a development of Leslie Lamport’s  LaTeX 2.09 (https://ctan.org/pkg/latex209) , 
      and superseded the older system in June 1994. The basic distribution is catalogued separately, at latex-base 
      (https://ctan.org/pkg/latex-base) ; apart from a large set of contributed packages and third-party 
      documentation (elsewhere on the archive), the distribution includes:

      – a bunch of  required packages (https://ctan.org/pkg/required) , which LaTeX authors are “entitled 
      to assume” will be present on any system running LaTeX; and
– a minimal set of documentation detailing 
      differences from the ‘old’ version of LaTeX in the areas of user commands (https://ctan.org/pkg/usrguide) , font 
      selection and control (https://ctan.org/pkg/fntguide) , class and package writing (https://ctan.org/pkg/clsguide) , font 
      encodings (https://ctan.org/pkg/encguide) , configuration options (https://ctan.org/pkg/cfgguide) and modification 
      of LaTeX (https://ctan.org/pkg/modguide) .

      For downloading details, see the linked catalogue entries above.
