UR  - https://ctan.org/pkg/linegoal
Y3  - 2025-02-07
T1  - linegoal
T2  - A “dimen” that returns the space left on the line
AU  - Chervet, Florent
AB  - (no language specified) The linegoal package provides a macro  \linegoal to be used with \setlength :
 \setlength< 'some 
      dimen' >\linegoal 
will set < 'some dimen' > to the horizontal length of the remainder 
      of the line.

      This is achieved using the  \pdfsavepos primitive of pdfTeX, through the zref-savepos (https://ctan.org/pkg/zref) package.

      Example:
 |
Some text: \begin{tabularx}\linegoal{|l|X|} \hline
one & two \\
three & four \\\hline
\end{tabularx}
| will position the table after the initial text, and make the table fill the rest of the line.
