TY  - ICOMM
UR  - https://ctan.org/pkg/longdivision
Y3  - 2025-02-07
T1  - longdivision
T2  - Typesets long division
AU  - Chatham, Hood
Y2  - 2023-10-21
PY  - 2023
AB  - (no language specified) This package executes the long division algorithm and typesets the solutions. The dividend must be a 
      positive decimal number and the divisor must be a positive integer. Repeating decimals is handled correctly, 
      putting a bar over the repeated part of the decimal. Dividends up to 20 digits long are handled gracefully 
      (though the typeset result will take up about a page), and dividends between 20 and 60 digits long slightly 
      less gracefully.

      The package defines two macros,  \longdivision and \intlongdivision . Each takes two arguments, 
      a dividend and a divisor. \longdivision keeps dividing until the remainder is zero, or it encounters 
      a repeated remainder. \intlongdivision stops when the dividend stops (though the dividend doesn’t 
      have to be an integer).

      This package depends on the  xparse (https://ctan.org/pkg/xparse) package from the l3packages 
      (https://ctan.org/pkg/l3packages) bundle.
