      Just as with  xparse (https://ctan.org/pkg/xparse) , it is possible to use a special syntax consisting 
      of single letters to express the arguments of a macro. However, lparse is able to read arguments 
      regardless of the macro system used — whether LaTeX, or ConTeXt, or even plain TeX. Of course, LuaTeX 
      must always be used as the engine.
