Y3  - 2025-02-09
T1  - luaoptions
T2  - Option handling for LuaLaTeX packages
AU  - Peron, Jacques
Y2  - 2022-10-30
PY  - 2022
AB  - (no language specified) This LuaLaTeX package provides extensive support for handling  'options' , on package level and 
      locally. It allows the declaration of sets of options, along with defaults, expected/allowed values and 
      limited type checking. These options can be enforced as package options, changed at any point during 
      a document, or overwritten locally by optional macro arguments. It is also possible to instantiate an 
      Options object as an independent Lua object, without linking it to a package. Luaoptions can be 
      used to enforce and prepopulate options, or it can be used to simply handle the parsing of optional key=value arguments 
      into proper Lua tables.
