Y3  - 2025-02-09
T1  - luaplot
T2  - Plotting graphs using Lua
AU  - Chetan Shirore and Ajit Kumar
Y2  - 2023-11-17
PY  - 2023
AB  - (no language specified) This package uses Lua to plot graphs of real-valued functions of a real variable in LaTeX. It furthermore 
      makes use of the  MetaPost (https://ctan.org/pkg/metapost) system as well as the luamplib (https://ctan.org/pkg/luamplib) and luacode 
      (https://ctan.org/pkg/luacode) packages. It provides an easy way for plotting graphs of standard mathematical 
      functions.

      There is no particular environment in the package for plotting graphs. It also works inside LaTeX floating 
      environments, like tables and figures. The compilation time for plotting several graphs in LaTeX using 
      this package is significantly less with the LuaLaTeX engine.

      The package is based on the core idea of loading mathematical functions inside Lua and determining plot 
      points using different methods available in Lua. After determining plot points in Lua, two different 
      approaches are used:

      + Pass plot points to the  MetaPost (https://ctan.org/pkg/metapost) system via luamplib (https://ctan.org/pkg/luamplib) .

      + Pass plot points to the  TikZ (https://ctan.org/pkg/pgf) package.
