AB  - (no language specified) The luaset package is developed to define finite sets and perform operations on them inside LaTeX documents. 
      There is no particular environment in the package for performing set operations. The package commands 
      can be used in any environment (including the mathematics environment). It is written in Lua, and the 
       .tex file is to be compiled with the LuaLaTeX engine. The time required for operations on sets 
      is not an issue while compiling with the LuaLaTeX engine. There is no need to install Lua on the users 
      system as TeX distributions (TeX Live or MikTeX) come bundled with LuaLaTeX.
