AU  - Kohm, Markus
AB  - (no language specified) The standard letter class  letter (https://ctan.org/pkg/letter) has a label feature. You can activate 
      it using \makelabels . While in Germany window envelopes are common, printing labels is not common, 
      and scrlttr2 (https://ctan.org/pkg/scrlttr2) has never supported label printing.

      Using  makelabels.lco does implement a \makelabels feature similar to the standard letter 
      classes. Currently there are (almost) no configuration features for makelabels.lco . But you may 
      use the envlab (https://ctan.org/pkg/envlab) package after loading makelabels.lco to get 
      various configuration features.
