T1  - mathtex
T2  - A CGI program to use LaTeX to put mathematics on the web
AU  - Forkosh, John
Y2  - 2014-12-06
PY  - 2014
AB  - (no language specified) MathTeX is a CGI program, written in C, that uses LaTeX and either dvipng or dvips/convert to emit GIF 
      or PNG images of LaTeX mathematical expressions. Users can put mathematics directly in html pages with 
      an <img> tag of the form
 <img src="/cgi-bin/mathtex.cgi?f(x)=\int_{-\infty}^xe^{-t^2}dt"> 
(see 
      the package home page for a complete discussion).

      MathTeX is a successor of the author's earlier  mimeTeX (https://ctan.org/pkg/mimetex) ; but mathTeX 
      uses real LaTeX, where as mimeTeX uses its own built-in fonts, interpreter and rendering engine. Users 
      who have LaTeX available on their server can obtain higher quality images and full LaTeX support with 
      mathTeX. Users whose server doesn't offer LaTeX can continue to use mimeTeX. The two programs are “plug-compatible”, 
      using the same <img> tag “user interface”, so migration is trivial.

      The package home page carries extensive documentation of MathTeX.
