      using TikZ (https://ctan.org/pkg/pgf) . For example, the MO diagram of dihydrogen would be written 
      as:

       \begin{MOdiagram} 
 \atom{left}{ 1s = {0;up} } 
 \atom{right}{ 1s = {0;up} } 
 \molecule{ 
      1sMO = {1;pair, } } 
 \end{MOdiagram} 

      The package also needs the  l3kernel (https://ctan.org/pkg/l3kernel) and l3packages (https://ctan.org/pkg/l3packages) bundles 
      from the LaTeX 3 experimental distribution.
