T2  - Make a format containing a document’s preamble
AU  - Carlisle, David
Y2  - 2020-10-23
PY  - 2020
AB  - (no language specified) The file  mylatex.ltx permits you to create a format that pre-loads a set of package files (and/or 
      other macros) that you regularly use. In some circumstances, this can be a great advantage (though on 
      an ordinarily fast modern computer on the desktop, gains will be limited).

      The general scheme is to initialise your usage by a command of the form:
 latex -ini mylatex.ltx 
      <document> 
whick will create a format file mylatex.fmt , which you then use as:
 latex 
      -fmt=mylatex <document>
