T1  - Nath
T2  - Natural mathematics notation
AU  - Marvan, Michal
AB  - (no language specified) Nath is a LaTeX (both 2e and 2.09) style to separate presentation and content in mathematical typography. 
      The style delivers a particular context-dependent presentation on the basis of a rather coarse context-independent 
      notation. Highlighted features: depending on the context, the command  \frac produces either built-up 
      or case or solidus fractions, with parentheses added whenever required for preservation of the mathematical 
      meaning; delimiters adapt their size to the material enclosed, rendering \left and \right almost 
      obsolete.
