T2  - Layout graphic rich documents
AU  - Bartels, Friedemann
Y2  - 2024-07-31
PY  - 2024
AB  - (no language specified) The pagelayout class enables you to layout pages declaratively using simple macros for pages, covers, 
      grids, templates, text, and graphics to create graphic rich, perfectly typeset, and print ready PDFs.

      The integration of  Inkscape (https://inkscape.org) allows you to create box shadows.

      The integration of  ImageMagick (https://imagemagick.org) allows you to configure compression and 
      sharpening for bitmap graphics to export web, print or preview versions of your document. Parallelized 
      image optimization, caching, and a draft mode enable fast PDF creation and a responsive workflow, even 
      for large documents with lots of photos and graphics.

      The pagelayout class also integrates the  PGF/TikZ (https://ctan.org/pkg/pgf) and tcolorbox 
      (https://ctan.org/pkg/tcolorbox) LaTeX packages.
