T1  - pagesLTS
T2  - Variants of last page labels
AU  - Münch, Hans-Martin
Y2  - 2025-06-05
PY  - 2025
AB  - (no language specified) The package was designed as an extension of the  lastpage (https://ctan.org/pkg/lastpage) package 
      — as well as that package’s LastPage label (created in hook enddocument/afterlastpage , formerly \AtEndDocument ) 
      it adds a VeryLastPage (created in the same hook, but formerly \AfterLastShipout ).

      When more than one page numbering scheme is in operation (as in a  book class document with frontmatter), 
      the labels above do not give the total number of pages, so the package also provides labels pagesLTS.< 'numbering 
      scheme' > , where the 'numbering scheme' is arabic , roman , etc.

      The package relies on the  undolabl (https://ctan.org/pkg/undolabl) package.

      Note: The “LTS” of the package name stands for: “L” = number of  'L' ast page, “T” = 'T' otal 
      number of pages, “S” = page numbering 'S' chemes (roman, arabic, ...)
