T1  - perpage
T2  - Make a counter reset at every page boundary
AU  - Kastrup, David
AB  - (no language specified) The package provides a mechanism to reset counters per page and/or keep their occurences sorted in order 
      of appearance on the page.

      The package also defines a command  \MakePerPage that designates a counter to be reset per page. 
      For example \MakePerPage[2]{footnote} will cause footnote numbers to start at 2 at the start of 
      every page (the optional argument defaults to 1). The machanism may require multiple passes to work; 
      LaTeX gives the usual changed label warning if this is necessary.

      The package is distributed as part of the  bigfoot (https://ctan.org/pkg/bigfoot) bundle.
