UR  - https://ctan.org/pkg/pgfmath-xfp
Y3  - 2025-08-31
T1  - pgfmath-xfp
T2  - Define pgfmath functions using xfp
AU  - Spratte, Jonathan P.
Y2  - 2025-01-11
PY  - 2025
AB  - (no language specified) This package allows to define  pgfmath (https://ctan.org/pkg/pgf) functions that use the xfp 
      (https://ctan.org/pkg/xfp) fpu for their calculations.

      The input arguments are parsed with  pgfmath (https://ctan.org/pkg/pgf) (while the pgf (https://ctan.org/pkg/pgf) -fpu 
      is locally active), and the results are forwarded to xfp (https://ctan.org/pkg/xfp) ’s fpu for 
      the function evaluation. The result of that calculation is then parsed by pgfmath again (with the surrounding 
      settings of pgfmath). This way the functions should be usable in every pgfmath context, though there 
      is some overhead to this approach.

      The package is only meant as a temporary stopgap until a more dedicated solution is available to use 
       xfp (https://ctan.org/pkg/xfp) in pgf (https://ctan.org/pkg/pgf) .
