AB  - (no language specified) PGFPlots draws high-quality function plots in normal or logarithmic scaling with a user-friendly interface 
      directly in TeX. The user supplies axis labels, legend entries and the plot coordinates for one or more 
      plots and PGFPlots applies axis scaling, computes any logarithms and axis ticks and draws the plots, 
      supporting line plots, scatter plots, piecewise constant plots, bar plots, area plots, mesh-- and surface 
      plots and some more.

      Pgfplots is based on  PGF/TikZ (https://ctan.org/pkg/pgf) (PGF); it runs equally for LaTeX/TeX/ConTeXt.
