T1  - phaistos
T2  - Disk of Phaistos font
AU  - Syropoulos, Apostolos
AB  - (no language specified) A font that contains all the symbols of the famous  Disc of Phaistos (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phaistos_Disc) , 
      together with a LaTeX package. The disc was ‘printed’ by stamping the wet clay with some sort of punches, 
      probably around 1700 BCE. The font is available in Adobe Type 1 and OpenType formats (the latter using 
      the Unicode positions for the symbols).

      There are those who believe that this Cretan script was used to ‘write’ Greek (it is known, for example, 
      that the rather later Cretan  Linear B (https://ctan.org/pkg/linearb) script was used to write 
      Greek), but arguments for other languages have been presented.
