AU  - Harders, Harald
AU  - Robertson, Will
AU  - Wilson, Peter R.
AB  - (no language specified) \printlength{length} prints the value of a LaTeX length in the units specified by \uselengthunit{unit} (‘unit’ 
      may be any TeX length unit except for scaled point, viz., any of: pt , pc , in , mm , cm , bp , dd or cc ). 
      When the unit is pt , the printed length value will include any stretch or shrink; otherwise these 
      are not printed. The ‘unit’ argument may also be PT , in which case length values will be printed 
      in point units but without any stretch or shrink values.
