AU  - Niepraschk, Rolf
AB  - (no language specified) This LaTeX package provides a way to use PostScript commands (e.g.,  PSTricks (https://ctan.org/pkg/pstricks-base) graphics, PSfrag 
      (https://ctan.org/pkg/psfrag) replacements, EPS graphics) inside a pdfLaTeX (https://ctan.org/pkg/pdftex) processed 
      document. You need recent versions of the LaTeX packages preview (https://ctan.org/pkg/preview-latex) , ifpdf 
      (https://ctan.org/pkg/ifpdf) , ifvtex (https://ctan.org/pkg/ifvtex) and a new LaTeX base installation. 
      All PostScript related commands, including `\usepackage', must be a parameter of the 'PSforPDF' macro. 
      For details see the test file 'ps4pdf-test.tex'. The PDF document is generated via dvips (https://ctan.org/pkg/dvips) and 
      ps2pdf.

      This package is now deprecated: it is recommended that users try  pst-pdf (https://ctan.org/pkg/pst-pdf) instead.
