T1  - rmligs
T2  - Remove incorrect ligatures in German documents
AU  - Jacke, Björn
AB  - (no language specified) Ligatures, which are a pleasing feature of TeX's use of fonts, should not be placed in German words between 
      the word stem and the rest of the word.

      The rmligs package is a perl script that takes input in ISO 8859-1 or -15, UTF-8 or LaTeX-style umlaut 
      encodings ( "a , "u , etc.), and inserts a break where an inappropriate ligature would appear. 
      So, for example, ‘Auflage’ will be changed to ‘Auf"|lage’, which typesets in a typographically correct 
      fashion.
