      subexpressions should be numbered. In standard LaTeX there is no provision for this. To solve this problem 
      Stephen Gildea once wrote  subeqn.sty for LaTeX 2.09 (https://ctan.org/pkg/latex209) ; Donald 
      Arsenau rewrote the macros and Johannes Braams made them available for LaTeX2e (https://ctan.org/pkg/latex) .

      Note that this package is not compatible with the package  subeqnarray (https://ctan.org/pkg/subeqnarray) (written 
      by Johannes Braams), but it can be used together with the LaTeX class options leqno and fleqn .
