AB  - (no language specified) \tabto{<length>} moves the typesetting position to <length> from the left margin of the 
      paragraph. If the typesetting position is already further along, \tabto starts a new line; the 
      command \tabto* will move position backwards if necessary, so that previous text may be overwritten.

      The command  \TabPositions may be used to define a set of tabbing positions, after which the command \tab advances 
      typesetting position to the next defined ‘tab stop’.
