AU  - Goodman, Donald P.
Y2  - 2018-12-08
PY  - 2018
AB  - (no language specified) TeX and LaTeX provide few facilities for dates by default, though many packages have filled this gap. 
      This package fills it, as well, with a pure TeX-primitive implementation. It can print dates, advance 
      them by numbers of days, weeks, or months, determine the weekday automatically (with an algorithm cribbed 
      from the  dayofweek.tex file written by Martin Minow), and print them in (mostly) arbitrary format. 
      It can also print calendars (monthly and yearly) automatically, and can be easily localized for non-English 
      languages.
