AB  - (no language specified) TeXshade is alignment shading software completely written in TeX/LaTeX; it can process multiple sequence 
      alignments in the  .MSF and the .ALN file formats. In addition to common shading algorithms, 
      it provides special shading modes showing functional aspects, e.g. charge or hydropathy, and a wide range 
      of commands for handling shading colours, text styles, labels, legends; it even allows the user to define 
      completely new shading modes. TeXshade combines highest flexibility with TeX output quality — all in 
      a bundle that does not demand excessive development time of the user.
