TY  - ICOMM
UR  - https://ctan.org/pkg/transparent-io
Y3  - 2025-06-29
T1  - Transparent-IO
T2  - Show for approval the filenames used in \input, \openin, or \openout
AU  - Wermuth, Udo
Y2  - 2022-04-30
PY  - 2022
AB  - (no language specified) This package provides macros to make the file I/O in plain TeX more transparent. That is, every  |\input| , |\openin| , and |\openout| operation by TeX is presented to the user who must check carefully if the file name of the source is acceptable. The user must sometimes enter additional text and has to specify the file name that the TeX operation should use.

      The macros require a complex installation procedure; the package contains  sed and bash scripts 
      to do this on a UNIX-like operating system. Every installation is different from any other as password-protected 
      macro names and private messages have to be chosen by the installer. Therefore, the files in the package 
      cannot be used directly. The files carry the extension .org , and only after the user has performed 
      an individual customization for a private installation the changed files are renamed and have the extension .tex . 
      For details see the manual.
UR  - https://ctan.org/tex-archive/macros/plain/contrib/transparent-io/README
UR  - https://ctan.org/tex-archive/macros/plain/contrib/transparent-io/Transparent-IO-doc.pdf
