AB  - (no language specified) In the year 2010, Randall Munroe on  posted a really funny and nice article (https://blog.xkcd.com/2010/05/03/color-survey-results/) on xkcd 
      (https://xkcd.com/) . He made a very curious experiment: showing colors to a lot of people and asking 
      to name each one.

      Afterward, he processed the data and sorted the names for each color by popularity — that means, how 
      many people gave the same name to the same color.

      This package makes the collected color names usable with LaTeX.
